(window.RW_DISPLAY = window.RW_DISPLAY || {})["transitions_1"] = [{"id":"0839a4b9","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"The Coastal Futures Conservatory in Virginia is known for creating aural representations of ecological data. One such effort combines underwater audio recorded in seagrass beds with data that track rising carbon levels in the seagrass. As carbon levels increase, the audio is correspondingly distorted; ______ listeners can “hear” the changes in the carbon levels.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The Coastal Futures Conservatory in Virginia is known for creating aural representations of ecological data. One such effort combines","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"underwater audio recorded in seagrass beds with data that track rising carbon levels in the seagrass. As carbon levels increase, the audio is","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"correspondingly distorted; ______ listeners can “hear” the changes in the carbon levels.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["furthermore,","by comparison,","for instance,","thus,"]},{"id":"edf30612","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"In the late twentieth century, scholars directed much discussion toward issues of spatiality. Adherents to quantitative analytical approaches delineated space with the use of GIS spatial technologies; ______ cultural geographer Doreen Massey defined space as the product of “an ever- shifting social geometry of power and signification,” focusing instead on socio-political forces.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["for example,","by contrast,","as such,","likewise,"]},{"id":"e0bd4f8a","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"In 1942, the 1,500-mile Alaska Highway was constructed in under nine months, largely due to the skilled work of nearly 4,000 African American soldiers from US Army engineering regiments. The soldiers contribution was overlooked for decades. ______ in 2017, lawmakers declared October 25 a day of recognition —“Alaska Highway Day”— for the troops who helped build this critical roadway.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In 1942, the 1,500-mile Alaska Highway was constructed in under nine months, largely due to the skilled work of nearly 4,000 African American","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"soldiers from US Army engineering regiments. The soldiers’ contribution was overlooked for decades. ______ in 2017, lawmakers declared","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"October 25 a day of recognition—“Alaska Highway Day”—for the troops who helped build this critical roadway.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Lastly,","Then,","Similarly,","For example,"]},{"id":"480ade7e","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"In response to adverse environmental conditions, many plants produce abscisic acid (ABA), a stress hormone. ABA triggers a slowdown in the biological processes of most plants. ______ when the mustard plant Schrenkiella parvula produces ABA in response to an environmental stressor, the hormone triggers accelerated growth.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In response to adverse environmental conditions, many plants produce abscisic acid (ABA), a stress hormone. ABA triggers a slowdown in the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"biological processes of most plants. ______ when the mustard plant Schrenkiella parvula produces ABA in response to an environmental stressor,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the hormone triggers accelerated growth.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Moreover,","In contrast,","For example,","Thus,"]},{"id":"3a715eca","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"In retrospect, one of the lessons of the 2003 Human Genome Project is that a gene is affected by many factors, not the least of which is its interactions with the protein products of other genes. ______ rather than just focusing on the human genome, efforts to better understand gene mutations related to disease have begun to consider the human proteome, the complete set of proteins expressed by human genes.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In retrospect, one of the lessons of the 2003 Human Genome Project is that a gene is affected by many factors, not the least of which is its","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"interactions with the protein products of other genes. ______ rather than just focusing on the human genome, efforts to better understand gene","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"mutations related to disease have begun to consider the human proteome, the complete set of proteins expressed by human genes.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["In other words,","That said,","For example,","Accordingly,"]},{"id":"b8eec031","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Researchers Helena Mihaljević-Brandt, Lucía Santamaría, and Marco Tullney report that while mathematicians may have traditionally worked alone, evidence points to a shift in the opposite direction. ______ mathematicians are choosing to collaborate with their peers — a trend illustrated by a rise in the number of mathematics publications credited to multiple authors.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Similarly,","For this reason,","Furthermore,","Increasingly,"]},{"id":"17e49403","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"When, in the 1800s, geologists first realized that much of Earth had once been covered by great sheets of ice, some theorized that the phenomenon was cyclical, occurring at regular intervals. Each Ice Age is so destructive, though, that it largely erases the geological evidence of its predecessor. ______ geologists were unable to confirm the theory of cyclical Ice Ages until the 1960s.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"When, in the 1800s, geologists first realized that much of Earth had once been covered by great sheets of ice, some theorized that the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"phenomenon was cyclical, occurring at regular intervals. Each Ice Age is so destructive, though, that it largely erases the geological evidence of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"its predecessor. ______ geologists were unable to confirm the theory of cyclical Ice Ages until the 1960s.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Hence,","Moreover,","Nevertheless,","Next,"]},{"id":"20733eac","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"It has long been thought that humans first crossed a land bridge into the Americas approximately 13,000 years ago. ______ based on radiocarbon dating of samples uncovered in Mexico, a research team recently suggested that humans may have arrived more than 30,000 years ago — much earlier than previously thought.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"It has long been thought that humans first crossed a land bridge into the Americas approximately 13,000 years ago. ______ based on radiocarbon","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"dating of samples uncovered in Mexico, a research team recently suggested that humans may have arrived more than 30,000 years ago—much","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"earlier than previously thought.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["As a result,","Similarly,","However,","In conclusion,"]},{"id":"60917233","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"In the 1880s, inventor Lewis Latimer improved upon Thomas Edison’s design for the electric light bulb. ______ Latimer made the light bulb more durable by placing cardboard around its carbon filament. With this innovation, Latimer became the first Black inventor to contribute to the electrification of the world.","question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Soon,","Regardless,","However,","Specifically,"]},{"id":"9e34720b","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Although those who migrated to California in 1849 dreamed of finding gold nuggets in streambeds, the state’s richest deposits were buried deeply in rock, beyond the reach of individual prospectors. ______ by 1852, many had given up their fortune-hunting dreams and gone to work for one of the large companies capable of managing California’s complex mining operations.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Although those who migrated to California in 1849 dreamed of finding gold nuggets in streambeds, the state’s richest deposits were buried","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"deeply in rock, beyond the reach of individual prospectors. ______ by 1852, many had given up their fortune-hunting dreams and gone to work for","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"one of the large companies capable of managing California’s complex mining operations.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Furthermore,","Still,","Consequently,","Next,"]},{"id":"2b5e0731","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"With darkness falling, a mother elephant loses sight of her calf and wants to make sure it is safe. ______ she releases an infrasonic call for the calf to hear. Infrasonic sound is below the range of human hearing, but many animals can hear these sounds from several miles away.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"With darkness falling, a mother elephant loses sight of her calf and wants to make sure it is safe. ______ she releases an infrasonic call for the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"calf to hear. Infrasonic sound is below the range of human hearing, but many animals can hear these sounds from several miles away.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["For example,","For this reason,","Nowadays,","Similarly,"]},{"id":"e3edc138","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"In a heated debate in biogeography, the field is divided between dispersalists and vicariancists. ______ there are those who argue that dispersal is the most crucial determining factor in a species’ distribution, and those who insist that vicariance (separation due to geographic barriers) is. Biogeographer Isabel Sanmartín counts herself among neither.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In a heated debate in biogeography, the field is divided between dispersalists and vicariancists. ______ there are those who argue that dispersal is","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"the most crucial determining factor in a species’ distribution, and those who insist that vicariance (separation due to geographic barriers) is.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Biogeographer Isabel Sanmartín counts herself among neither.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Furthermore,","By contrast,","Similarly,","That is,"]},{"id":"d54e16ee","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Originally coined by economist Joan Robinson to refer to markets with multiple sellers of a product but only one buyer, the term “monopsony” can also refer to markets where demand for labor is limited. In a product monopsony, the single buyer can force sellers to lower their prices. ______ in a labor monopsony, employers can force workers to accept lower wages.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Originally coined by economist Joan Robinson to refer to markets with multiple sellers of a product but only one buyer, the term “monopsony”","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"can also refer to markets where demand for labor is limited. In a product monopsony, the single buyer can force sellers to lower their prices.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"______ in a labor monopsony, employers can force workers to accept lower wages.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Earlier,","Instead,","Similarly,","In particular,"]},{"id":"2df7b582","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Plato believed material objects to be crude representations of unseen ideal forms. In his view, such abstract, nonmaterial forms are the ultimate source of knowledge. Aristotle disagreed, positing that knowledge is best obtained through direct engagement with the material world; ______ sensory experience of the material is the ultimate source of knowledge.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Plato believed material objects to be crude representations of unseen ideal forms. In his view, such abstract, nonmaterial forms are the ultimate","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"source of knowledge. Aristotle disagreed, positing that knowledge is best obtained through direct engagement with the material world; ______","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"sensory experience of the material is the ultimate source of knowledge.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["regardless,","admittedly,","in other words,","meanwhile,"]},{"id":"db8fe023","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"A potter choosing which type of clay to use for a piece considers two key factors: the desired look of the piece and its intended use. ______ earthenware clay is often used for decorative pieces because of its rustic look. This type of clay is not often used in industrial settings, though, because it is less durable than other clays.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"A potter choosing which type of clay to use for a piece considers two key factors: the desired look of the piece and its intended use. ______","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"earthenware clay is often used for decorative pieces because of its rustic look. This type of clay is not often used in industrial settings, though,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"because it is less durable than other clays.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["In other words,","Regardless,","In conclusion,","For example,"]},{"id":"47547d07","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"In June, female loggerhead sea turtles will swim back to the sandy beaches where they were born to lay eggs of their own. First, the turtle will dig her nest in the sand. ______ she will lay up to 100 eggs in the nest. Finally, she will cover it all with sand, before returning to the ocean.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In June, female loggerhead sea turtles will swim back to the sandy beaches where they were born to lay eggs of their own. First, the turtle will dig","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"her nest in the sand. ______ she will lay up to 100 eggs in the nest. Finally, she will cover it all with sand, before returning to the ocean.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["By contrast,","Similarly,","Next,","For example,"]}];
